[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m ### Step 2: Use vector or coordinate geometry
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Let’s place the triangle in the coordinate plane with:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - $ O $ (circumcenter) at the origin
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - $ I $ (incenter) at some point in the plane
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - $ A $ is a vertex of the triangle
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m We are told that $ \overline{IA} \perp \overline{OI} $, i.e., the vectors $ \vec{IA} $ and $ \vec{OI} $ are perpendicular.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Let’s denote:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - $ \vec{I} = \vec{i} $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - $ \vec{A} = \vec{a} $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - $ \vec{O} = \vec{0} $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Then:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m \vec{IA} = \vec{a} - \vec{i}, \quad \vec{OI} = \vec{i}
