[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m ### Step 1: Understand the Geometry of the Rhombus
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m In a **rhombus**, the diagonals **bisect each other at right angles** (not necessarily in general, but in this case, they **do** intersect at the origin, and the diagonals are perpendicular). So, the diagonals intersect at the origin and are perpendicular.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
