[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m > Find the sum of all integer bases $ b > 9 $ for which $ 17_{b} $ is a divisor of $ 97_{b} $.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m ### Step 1: Understand the notation
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m In base $ b $, the number $ 17_b $ means:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 17_b = 1 \cdot b + 7 = b + 7
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Similarly,
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 97_b = 9 \cdot b + 7 = 9b + 7
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m We are told that $ 17_b $ divides $ 97_b $, i.e.,
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 9b + 7 \equiv 0 \pmod{b + 7}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m This is equivalent to:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 9b + 7 \equiv 0 \pmod{b + 7}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m ### Step 2: Use modular arithmetic
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m We want to find when:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 9b + 7 \equiv 0 \pmod{b + 7}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Let’s simplify the expression:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 9b + 7 \equiv 0 \pmod{b + 7}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m We can write this as:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 9b + 7 = k(b + 7) \quad \text{for some integer } k
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Let’s compute $ 9b + 7 $ modulo $ b + 7 $:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 9b + 7 = 9(b + 7) - 63 + 7 = 9(b + 7) - 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 9b + 7 \equiv -56 \pmod{b + 7}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m But we are told that this is congruent to 0:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m -56 \equiv 0 \pmod{b + 7}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m b + 7 \mid 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m ### Step 3: Find all bases $ b > 9 $ such that $ b + 7 \mid 56 $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m We need to find all divisors of 56 that are greater than $ 9 - 7 = 2 $, and then subtract 7 from each to get $ b $.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m First, find all positive divisors of 56:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 56 = 2^3 \cdot 7
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Divisors of 56 are:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 1, 2, 4, 7, 8, 14, 28, 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Now, we want $ b + 7 $ to be one of these, and $ b > 9 $, so:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m b + 7 > 10 \Rightarrow b > 3
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m So we consider the divisors of 56 greater than 3:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 8, 14, 28, 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Now subtract 7 from each:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - $ 8 - 7 = 1 $ → $ b = 1 $ ❌ (not > 9)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - $ 14 - 7 = 7 $ → $ b = 7 $ ❌ (not > 9)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - $ 28 - 7 = 21 $ → $ b = 21 $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - $ 56 - 7 = 49 $ → $ b = 49 $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m So the valid values of $ b $ are:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m b = 21, 49
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m ### Step 4: Sum the valid bases
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 21 + 49 = 70
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
