[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - Incenter $ I $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - $ \overline{IA} \perp \overline{OI} $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - Circumradius $ R = 13 $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - Inradius $ r = 6 $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - We are to find $ AB \cdot AC $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m ### Step 1: Use the given condition $ \overline{IA} \perp \overline{OI} $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m This means that the vector $ \vec{IA} $ is perpendicular to the vector $ \vec{OI} $.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Let’s denote:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - $ \vec{IA} = \vec{A} - \vec{I} $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - $ \vec{OI} = \vec{I} - \vec{O} $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Then the dot product:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m \vec{IA} \cdot \vec{OI} = 0
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m (\vec{A} - \vec{I}) \cdot (\vec{I} - \vec{O}) = 0
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m This is a vector equation, but it can be interpreted geometrically in triangle geometry.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m ### Step 2: Use known triangle identities
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m We are given:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - $ R = 13 $, the circumradius
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - $ r = 6 $, the inradius
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - $ \overline{IA} \perp \overline{OI} $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m We want to find $ AB \cdot AC $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Let’s denote:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - $ AB = c $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - $ AC = b $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - $ BC = a $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Then we want to find $ b \cdot c $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m We also know that in any triangle:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m AB \cdot AC = bc
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m We can use the formula for the inradius:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m r = \frac{A}{s}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Where:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - $ A $ is the area of the triangle
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - $ s = \frac{a + b + c}{2} $ is the semi-perimeter
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Also, the circumradius is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m R = \frac{abc}{4A}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m So we have:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
