[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - When she walks at speed **$ s + 2 $** km/h, the total time is **2 hours and 24 minutes** (which is **2.4 hours**).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - We are to find the **time** it takes her to walk at speed **$ s + \frac{1}{2} $** km/h, including the **$ t $** minutes spent in the coffee shop.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m ### Step 1: Set up equations based on the given information
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Let’s denote:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - $ t $ = time (in minutes) spent in the coffee shop
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - $ s $ = walking speed (in km/h)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - Total time for walk (including $ t $ minutes) = 4 hours = 240 minutes
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m #### First scenario:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - Walking speed: $ s $ km/h
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - Distance: 9 km
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - Time taken: $ \frac{9}{s} $ hours = $ \frac{9}{s} \times 60 $ minutes = $ \frac{540}{s} $ minutes
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - Total time: $ \frac{540}{s} + t = 240 $ minutes
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m #### Second scenario:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - Walking speed: $ s + 2 $ km/h
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - Distance: 9 km
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - Time taken: $ \frac{9}{s + 2} \times 60 $ minutes = $ \frac{540}{s + 2} $ minutes
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - Total time: $ \frac{540}{s + 2} + t = 2.4 \times 60 = 144 $ minutes
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m ### Step 2: Set up two equations
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m From the first scenario:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m \frac{540}{s} + t = 240 \tag{1}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m From the second scenario:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m \frac{540}{s + 2} + t = 144 \tag{2}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m ### Step 3: Subtract equation (2) from equation (1)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m \left( \frac{540}{s} + t \right) - \left( \frac{540}{s + 2} + t \right) = 240 - 144
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m \frac{540}{s} - \frac{540}{s + 2} = 96
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Factor out 540:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 540 \left( \frac{1}{s} - \frac{1}{s + 2} \right) = 96
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Compute the difference of fractions:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m \frac{1}{s} - \frac{1}{s + 2} = \frac{(s + 2) - s}{s(s + 2)} = \frac{2}{s(s + 2)}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 540 \cdot \frac{2}{s(s + 2)} = 96
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m \frac{1080}{s(s + 2)} = 96
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Multiply both sides by $ s(s + 2) $:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 1080 = 96s(s + 2)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Divide both sides by 24:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 45 = 4s(s + 2)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Expand the right-hand side:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 45 = 4s^2 + 8s
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Bring all terms to one side:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 4s^2 + 8s - 45 = 0
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m ### Step 4: Solve the quadratic equation
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Use the quadratic formula:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m s = \frac{-8 \pm \sqrt{8^2 - 4(4)(-45)}}{2(4)}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m s = \frac{-8 \pm \sqrt{64 + 720}}{8}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m s = \frac{-8 \pm \sqrt{784}}{8}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m s = \frac{-8 \pm 28}{8}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m We discard the negative root (speed cannot be negative), so:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m s = \frac{-8 + 28}{8} = \frac{20}{8} = \frac{5}{2} = 2.5 \text{ km/h}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m ### Step 5: Find $ t $ using equation (1)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m \frac{540}{s} + t = 240
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
