[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m ### **Step 2: Set up equations based on distance, speed, and time**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Let’s denote:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - Distance = 9 km
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - Speed = $ s $ km/h
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - Time = 4 hours (including $ t $ minutes)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m So, the time in hours is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m \text{Time} = 4 \text{ hours}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m But the time spent walking is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m \text{Time walking} = \frac{9}{s} \text{ hours}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m The time spent in the coffee shop is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m t = 4 - \frac{9}{s} \text{ hours}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m But $ t $ is in **minutes**, so we need to convert it to hours:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
