[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m But we are told that this is congruent to 0 modulo $ b + 7 $, so:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m -56 \equiv 0 \pmod{b + 7}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m This implies that:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m b + 7 \mid 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m ### Step 3: Find all $ b > 9 $ such that $ b + 7 \mid 56 $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m We now find all divisors of 56, and then subtract 7 to get $ b $, and check if $ b > 9 $.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m The divisors of 56 are:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 1, 2, 4, 7, 8, 14, 28, 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Now, subtract 7 from each to get $ b $:
