[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - She walks at a constant speed of **$ s $ kilometers per hour**.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - The total time for the walk (including the time spent in the coffee shop) is **4 hours**, and the time spent in the coffee shop is **$ t $ minutes**.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - When she walks at **$ s + 2 $** kilometers per hour, the total time is **2 hours and 24 minutes**, and the time spent in the coffee shop is still **$ t $ minutes**.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - We are to find the **time** it takes her to walk at **$ s + \frac{1}{2} $** kilometers per hour, including the $ t $ minutes spent in the coffee shop.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m ### Step 1: Convert all times to hours
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Let’s convert the time spent in the coffee shop from minutes to hours:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - $ t $ minutes = $ \frac{t}{60} $ hours
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m ### Step 2: Set up equations based on the given information
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m #### Case 1: Walking at speed $ s $ km/h
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Time taken = $ \frac{9}{s} $ hours
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Total time = time walking + time in coffee shop = $ \frac{9}{s} + \frac{t}{60} = 4 $ hours
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m \frac{9}{s} + \frac{t}{60} = 4 \tag{1}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m #### Case 2: Walking at speed $ s + 2 $ km/h
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Time taken = $ \frac{9}{s + 2} $ hours
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Total time = $ \frac{9}{s + 2} + \frac{t}{60} = 2 + \frac{24}{60} = 2.4 $ hours
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m \frac{9}{s + 2} + \frac{t}{60} = 2.4 \tag{2}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m ### Step 3: Solve the system of equations
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m We now have two equations:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 1. $ \frac{9}{s} + \frac{t}{60} = 4 $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 2. $ \frac{9}{s + 2} + \frac{t}{60} = 2.4 $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Subtract equation (2) from equation (1):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m \left( \frac{9}{s} + \frac{t}{60} \right) - \left( \frac{9}{s + 2} + \frac{t}{60} \right) = 4 - 2.4
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m \frac{9}{s} - \frac{9}{s + 2} = 1.6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Factor out the 9:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 9 \left( \frac{1}{s} - \frac{1}{s + 2} \right) = 1.6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 9 \left( \frac{(s + 2) - s}{s(s + 2)} \right) = 1.6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 9 \left( \frac{2}{s(s + 2)} \right) = 1.6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m \frac{18}{s(s + 2)} = 1.6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Multiply both sides by $ s(s + 2) $:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 18 = 1.6 s(s + 2)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Divide both sides by 1.6:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m \frac{18}{1.6} = s(s + 2)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 11.25 = s(s + 2)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Now solve the quadratic equation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m s^2 + 2s - 11.25 = 0
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Use the quadratic formula:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m s = \frac{-2 \pm \sqrt{2^2 - 4(1)(-11.25)}}{2(1)} = \frac{-2 \pm \sqrt{4 + 45}}{2} = \frac{-2 \pm \sqrt{49}}{2}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m s = \frac{-2 \pm 7}{2}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m We discard the negative root (speed cannot be negative), so:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m s = \frac{-2 + 7}{2} = \frac{5}{2} = 2.5 \text{ km/h}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m ---
