[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m ### Step 1: Understand the Geometry of the Rhombus
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m In a rhombus, the diagonals are perpendicular bisectors of each other and intersect at the origin. Let the diagonals be $AC$ and $BD$, and let their intersection be the origin.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Let the coordinates of the vertices be:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - $A = (a, b)$
