[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m ### Step 3: Use the Rhombus Properties
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m In a rhombus, all sides are equal in length, and the diagonals are perpendicular. The diagonals $AC$ and $BD$ are perpendicular, so the product of their slopes is $-1$.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Let’s compute the slopes of the diagonals:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - Slope of $AC$: $\frac{-b - b}{-a - a} = \frac{-2b}{-2a} = \frac{b}{a}$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m - Slope of $BD$: $\frac{-d - d}{-c - c} = \frac{-2d}{-2c} = \frac{d}{c}$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
