[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Let’s place the triangle in the coordinate plane with the circumcenter $O$ at the origin, and the incenter $I$ at some point $(x, y)$. Then the vector $\overrightarrow{IA}$ is from $I$ to $A$, and the vector $\overrightarrow{OI}$ is from $O$ to $I$.
