[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m ### Step 3: Use the formula for the inradius
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m The inradius $ r $ of a triangle is given by:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m r = \frac{A}{s}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m where $ A $ is the area of the triangle, and $ s $ is the semi-perimeter:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m s = \frac{a + b + c}{2}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m So,
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m r = \frac{A}{s} \Rightarrow A = r \cdot s = 6s
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Also, the area $ A $ can be expressed using the circumradius $ R $ and the sides of the triangle:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m A = \frac{abc}{4R}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m So,
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 6s = \frac{abc}{4 \cdot 13} \Rightarrow 6s = \frac{abc}{52}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Thus,
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
