[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m So,
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m IA = \frac{r}{\sin \frac{A}{2}} = \frac{6}{\sin \frac{A}{2}}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Also, we are given that $ IA \perp OI $, so the angle between $ IA $ and $ OI $ is 90 degrees.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m We can now use the fact that:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m IA \perp OI \Rightarrow \vec{IA} \cdot \vec{OI} = 0
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m This is a vector condition, but we can use the fact that in a triangle, the incenter and circumcenter are related by the formula:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m OI^2 = R(R - 2r)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m And we have already computed $ OI = \sqrt{13} $, and $ R = 13 $, $ r = 6 $, so this is consistent.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Now, we can use the fact that:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m IA = \frac{r}{\sin \frac{A}{2}} = \frac{6}{\sin \frac{A}{2}}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m And we are given that $ IA \perp OI $, so the angle between $ IA $ and $ OI $ is 90 degrees.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m This implies that:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m \sin \frac{A}{2} = \frac{r}{IA} = \frac{6}{IA}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m So,
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m IA = \frac{6}{\sin \frac{A}{2}}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Now, we can use the formula for the area of the triangle:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m A = r \cdot s = 6s
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m Also,
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=25105)[0m $$
